counterexample:
-- No INSERT statements can produce a counterexample under the given schema.
-- Any valid test data (with distinct integer values) will make Q1 and Q2 return the same result.

-- For example, the following valid INSERTs yield identical answers:
INSERT INTO table1 (c1) VALUES (1);
INSERT INTO table1 (c1) VALUES (4);
INSERT INTO table1 (c1) VALUES (9);

-- Q1 will compute MIN(ABS(4-1), ABS(9-1), ABS(9-4)) = MIN(3,8,5) = 3
-- Q2 will compute differences between consecutive sorted values: ABS(4-1)=3 and ABS(9-4)=5, and MIN(3,5)=3
-- Thus, both queries return the same result and this data cannot serve as a counterexample.

