INSERT INTO table1 (c4, c2, c1, c3) VALUES (2, '2020-02-01', 40, 400);
-- (no row for '2020-02-02' for c4 = 2 so that group 2 contributes 0 in the numerator)

/*
For group 1: TEMP finds MIN(c2) = '2020-01-01'; then the join of TEMP with table1 (on c4) produces three rows for c4=1. The CASE expression gives 1 for each row where A.c2 = '2020-01-01' + 1 = '2020-01-02'. Since there are two such rows, the SUM is 2. The COUNT(DISTINCT TEMP.c4) is 1. So Q1 returns 2/1 = 2.00 for the overall fraction when combined with group 2 (which contributes 0), the average may be computed over groups yielding a different result.
For group 2: TEMP finds MIN(c2) = '2020-02-01' and only one row exists, but no next–day row exists so it adds 0.
Thus, over both groups, Q1 computes a total numerator of (2 + 0) and a denominator of 2, whereas Q2 will count at most one matching row per group (yielding 1 for group 1 and 0 for group 2) and so will produce (1 + 0)/2 = 0.50.
This difference in aggregation causes Q1 and Q2 to yield different FRACTION values.
*/

