Assume that despite the schema declaring c2 as DATE, the system sometimes stores a time component. 
Below we insert two rows with the same EXTRA and c1='REPORT'.
Row 1 has c2 = '2019-07-04' (i.e. '2019-07-04 00:00:00') and Row 2 has c2 = '2019-07-04 03:00:00'.
Q1, which uses an equality comparison to '2019-07-04', will include only Row 1, while Q2, which uses DATEDIFF, will include both rows.
*/

